  "description": "DUDXEG crystallizes in the trigonal crystal system with space group P -3 1 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C248 H168 Ce13 N54 O60 5+,C1 O3 2-,3(Cl1 1-),25(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 12 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce2C (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce2D (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce2E (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce3A (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce3B (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce3C (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce3D (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce3E (Ce) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 33 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.328-5.191 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 115.62-167.78°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula {[Ce13(H2O)6(phen)18(ccnm)6(CO3)14]·Cl3·CO3}·25(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
